{"title":"Fire Safety Engineer Roadmap","role":"Fire Safety Engineer","summary":"A Fire Safety Engineer designs, evaluates, implements, and maintains systems that prevent fires, protect people and property, and enable safe evacuation and emergency response.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Fire Technology & Safety Engineering"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Fire Safety Engineer designs, evaluates, implements, and maintains systems that prevent fires, protect people and property, and enable safe evacuation and emergency response."},{"type":"p","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fire science and fire dynamics"},{"text":"Fire prevention"},{"text":"Fire detection and alarm systems"},{"text":"Fire suppression systems"},{"text":"Emergency evacuation planning"},{"text":"Building and industrial fire safety"},{"text":"Hazard identification and risk assessment"},{"text":"Safety audits and inspections"},{"text":"Emergency preparedness"},{"text":"Fire protection engineering"},{"text":"Occupational and industrial safety"},{"text":"Regulatory compliance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Fire Safety Engineers can work across manufacturing plants, oil & gas, construction, commercial buildings, hospitals, airports, warehouses, data centers, power plants, hotels, infrastructure projects, and safety consulting."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Build fire science, safety engineering, risk assessment, fire protection and emergency-response fundamentals; enter as Fire Safety Engineer/Safety Engineer."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Fire Safety Engineer, Fire Protection Engineer, HSE Engineer or Safety Specialist."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Move into Fire & Safety Mana